ey features:**\n- **Semaphore-based concurrency control**: Limits tasks to `max_concurrent` running at once\n- **Graceful interrupt handling**: When you press Ctrl+C, the function:\n  1. Catches the `KeyboardInterrupt`\n  2. Cancels all pending tasks (injecting `CancelledError`)\n  3. Waits for all tasks to finish (allowing `try/finally` and context managers to run cleanup)\n  4. Re-raises the interrupt\n\nThis ensures that even if interrupted, each task's cleanup code (in `finally` blocks or async context managers) will execute before the program exits.\n\nYou can use it like:\n```python\nfrom run import run_tasks\n\nasync def some_task():\n    try:\n        # do work\n        pass\n    finally:\n        # cleanup code always runs\n        pass\n\nawait run_tasks([some_task, another_task], max_concurrent=5)\n```","ttft_ms":12792,"type":"result","duration_ms":15756,"uuid":"f68c07ba-7fef-459f-b09d-50fd06731299","ttft_stream_ms":994,"time_to_request_ms":78,"queued_turn_count":0}
